+
+## Local Network Access
+
+The app can reach resources on the user's loopback interface (`localhost`,
+`127.0.0.1`, `::1`) and private network (`10/8`, `172.16/12`, `192.168/16`,
+`*.local`) using Chrome's [Local Network Access](https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/local-network-access) feature:
+
+- `src/middleware.ts` sends `Permissions-Policy: local-network-access=(self)` on
+  every response, opting the origin into the feature.
+- `src/utils/localNetwork.ts` exports `fetchLocalNetwork()`, which sets the
+  `targetAddressSpace` fetch option (`loopback` or `local`, inferred from the
+  hostname when not given). This is what triggers the permission prompt and
+  allows an `http://` local target from the `https://` site.
+- `/local-network` is a demo page where you can enter a local URL, pick the
+  address space, and inspect the response. The current permission state is read
+  through `navigator.permissions.query({ name: 'local-network-access' })`.
